    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6545" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cantātrix</span></b> , īcis,
			f.
		adj.
		cantator (postclass.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Musical</i>, <i>singing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">choreae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. B. Gild. 448</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cantātrix</span></b> ,
			īcis, f., <i>a
				female singer</i>, <i><span class="en">Vulg. 2 Reg. 19, 35</span></i>; cf.
					<i><span class="en">Prisc. p. 1225</span></i>
			P.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Using enchantments</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">anus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 128, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aniculae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2</span></i>
			, p. 123, 25.</div>
